From: alex <49746433+Master-Yoba@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 21:57:42 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] renderer/vulkan: a texture tile in the right part of a
 surface is found in the surface cache

retrieve_color_surface_as_texture accepted a sub-rectangle of a cached
color surface only if address + stride * height stayed inside it. For a
linear texture the last row ends after width pixels, not a whole stride,
so a tile in the right-hand part of an atlas surface failed the check and
was read from guest memory, which holds the surface as of its last sync:
an older frame.

Soul Sacrifice Delta builds its bloom in such atlases and composites the
last tiles over the scene, so the bloom trailed moving objects by a frame
or more (the butterfly on the title, the book in the main menu).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 vita3k/renderer/src/vulkan/surface_cache.cpp | 9 +++++++--
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/vita3k/renderer/src/vulkan/surface_cache.cpp b/vita3k/renderer/src/vulkan/surface_cache.cpp
index 289bb6f4..8aa6203f 100644
--- a/vita3k/renderer/src/vulkan/surface_cache.cpp
+++ b/vita3k/renderer/src/vulkan/surface_cache.cpp
@@ -465,8 +465,13 @@ std::optional<TextureLookupResult> VKSurfaceCache::retrieve_color_surface_as_tex
         // about the strides, I've yet to see a case where the byte stride is different
         return std::nullopt;
 
-    // Check if we can use this surface
-    bool addr_in_range_of_cache = ((address + total_surface_size) <= (ite->first + info.total_bytes + 4));
+    // Check if we can use this surface. A linear texture ends with its last row's last pixel, not a
+    // whole stride further: a tile in the right part of an atlas surface (Soul Sacrifice Delta's bloom
+    // chain) would otherwise overrun it, and be read from memory as it was at the last sync
+    uint32_t texture_end_bytes = total_surface_size;
+    if (tiling == SurfaceTiling::Linear && original_height > 0)
+        texture_end_bytes = stride_bytes * (original_height - 1) + original_width * gxm::bits_per_pixel(base_format) / 8;
+    bool addr_in_range_of_cache = ((address + texture_end_bytes) <= (ite->first + info.total_bytes + 4));
 
     if (ite->first != address && !addr_in_range_of_cache)
